        "keyDetails": "Three details carry the scenario. The drug is an antiepileptic, so the omission carries a risk that persists after the missed doses. The error is yours and nobody else has noticed, so whether anyone finds out depends entirely on you. And he is well at the moment, which is exactly what makes keeping quiet tempting.",
        "reasoning": "[C] comes first because it removes the danger and gets senior input on the catch-up dose. [E] follows immediately: the candour duty applies because harm remains possible, and Mr Okafor needs the information to keep himself safe. [A] is important for the system but does not help him today. [D] and [B] both restart the drug, so the difference between them lies in honesty: [D] is a procedural shortcut that sidelines a colleague, while [B] is a choice to conceal.",
